{
  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "Limb (a) of the baseline no-show test is satisfied: the trip record for TRP-09101 carries a driver 'arrived' event at 2026-09-01T08:10:20+08:00, and the driver is the party who terminated the trip.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (b) is satisfied on the arrival geofence test. All 33 driver fixes sit 24.01 m from the pickup pin - min, mean and max are the same 24.01 m figure - well inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD zone class. The trace opens at 08:10:00, twenty seconds BEFORE the 08:10:20 'arrived' event, so the driver was inside the geofence at or before that event as the clause requires. Qualifying driver fixes number 33 of 33, so there are far more than the three consecutive in-radius readings POL-NS-02 demands.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01", "POL-NS-02"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (c) is satisfied. The driver's longest qualifying in-geofence run is 320 continuous seconds, from the first qualifying fix at 08:10:00 to the last at 08:15:20, against a STANDARD minimum dwell of 300 seconds. The derived shortfall is MINUS 20 seconds - that is, a 20 second surplus, not a shortfall. The point is robust even on the driver's own less favourable reading: measured from the 'arrived' marker at 08:10:20 to cancellation at 08:15:20 is exactly 300 seconds, still at the minimum. The dwell is measured from the first qualifying GPS fix, per the clause, and not from the arrival tap.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.arrival.longest_qualifying_run.duration_sec",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "Limb (d) is satisfied. The trip record shows the trip terminated by the driver at 08:15:20 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW - one of the three codes limb (d) expressly recognises - at the very moment the 320 second dwell elapsed, and it records no boarding event anywhere.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09101", "EV-GPS-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-01"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The arrival marker is TRUE, so POL-NS-05 does not displace the fee. At the arrived timestamp the trace reports a single distinct speed of 0.0 kph - the driver was stationary, not travelling - and his position was 24 m from the pin, roughly one twelfth of the 300 m distance threshold and nowhere near the 15 kph motion threshold. This is not a driver tapping 'arrived' while rolling down an expressway; it is a driver parked at the pickup point.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-05"],
      "relies_on": "derived.driver_track.distinct_speeds_kph",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-03 is not engaged. The driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue 400 m away, so the wrong-entrance route does not arise. Independently, the driver's in-app message at 08:10:35 states he is 'at the sheltered pickup point beside Block 310', and the trip record's registered pickup bears venue_id VEN-CLEMENTI-310 with the label 'Blk 310 Clementi Ave 4, sheltered pickup point'. That is a party statement in the chat log matching the registered venue, not an inference from geography.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-TRIP-09101", "EV-GPS-09101", "EV-CHAT-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-03"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "POL-NS-04 does not exonerate the rider, because limb (a) fails outright. The chat log for the waiting window contains no rider message at all: three messages only - the system notice 'Your driver has arrived' at 08:10:21, and two driver messages at 08:10:35 and 08:14:10. Limb (a) requires at least one locating or coordinating message FROM THE RIDER, and there is none. The message_count of 3 in the chat log also matches trip_record.chat_message_count of 3, so the log is not truncated.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-CHAT-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The rider's own track does not place them at the pickup point, and cannot support limb (c) of POL-NS-04 either. The rider track carries 15 fixes and rider_qualifying_fix_count is 0 of 15; every fix sits 519.37 m from the pin, far outside the 100 m STANDARD rider-presence radius. I put it precisely: whether those fixes are excluded because they fall outside the radius or are filtered for accuracy, limb (c) is at best undecidable and neutral and at worst affirmatively failed on admissible fixes - on no reading does it place the rider within 100 m of the pin. The rider's assertion that they were 'downstairs' is not borne out by their own device.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-04"],
      "relies_on": "derived.rider_presence.mean_distance_m",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "There is no waiting-period shortfall, so POL-NS-06 is not engaged and the fee is not refundable on that route. I disclose that the traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-09101-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT - no advisory matched this pickup road and waiting window. The driver does not rely on limb (i) accumulation and does not need to: the dwell was one single continuous in-geofence run of 320 seconds, so no advisory is required to join intervals together, and I assert nothing against the missing artifact.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-ADVIS-09101-01", "EV-GPS-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-06"],
      "asserted_weight": 0.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The money reconciles. The SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is the GREATER of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00) under fee_schedule.resolution_rule; the two dimensions agree, the fare breakdown's difference field reads 0.00, and no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises. The fee therefore stands as itemised.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-08", "POL-NS-01"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.schedule_fee",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No artifact that carries a deciding fact is impaired, so POL-NS-09(a) and (e) are not engaged. The trace is COMPLETE at weight 1.0: 100 per cent coverage, 33 fixes at a 10 second cadence equal to the expected interval, zero gaps and a maximum gap of 0 seconds. The 08:10:20 'arrived' event coincides exactly with a fix, so there is no clock skew under POL-NS-08(a); the log's 3 messages match the trip record, so there is no POL-NS-08(c) chat defect; and the fee reconciles under POL-NS-08(d). Deciding facts rest on clean, weight-1.0 artifacts.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-GPS-09101", "EV-CHAT-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101", "EV-FARE-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09", "POL-NS-08"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "No abuse or repeat-dispute trigger is present. rider_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0 and driver_profile.disputes_with_counterparty_90d is 0, so POL-NS-09(c) is not met; rider_profile.no_show_disputes_30d is 0, so POL-NS-09(d) is not met. I cite only the fields the clause names.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-RPROF-09101", "EV-DPROF-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-09"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "The driver is entitled to compensation. POL-NS-01 is satisfied in full and no clause from POL-NS-03 to POL-NS-06 displaces it, so POL-NS-07 pays the driver 80 per cent of the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee - SGD 3.20 - with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so the second limb is never reached and compensation is not withheld. I rely only on the two fields POL-NS-07 names, no_show_terminations_30d and completed_trips_30d; prior_no_show_flags is a lifetime counter and I do not use it.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09101", "EV-DPROF-09101", "EV-TRIP-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-NS-07"],
      "relies_on": "derived.money.driver_compensation",
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    },
    {
      "text": "On the charge itself the disposition is that the present state stands: fare_breakdown shows payment_status CHARGED and refund_issued_sgd 0.00, and the evidence does not support the rider's claim to have the charge reversed. Under POL-GEN-03 that is NO_ACTION on the fee, while the case as a whole produces DRIVER_COMPENSATION of SGD 3.20 in the driver's favour.",
      "evidence_ids": ["EV-FARE-09101"],
      "clause_ids": ["POL-GEN-03", "POL-NS-07"],
      "asserted_weight": 1.0
    }
  ]
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.20,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.20,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your request to reverse the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee is not supported on this record. All four limbs of POL-NS-01 hold. (a) The trip record carries a driver 'arrived' event at 08:10:20 for TRP-09101. (b) The GPS trace EV-GPS-09101 opens at 08:10:00 with a fix 24.01 m from the pickup pin, and every one of the driver's 33 fixes sits at that same 24.01 m — inside the 50 m STANDARD arrival radius and more than the three consecutive in-radius readings POL-NS-02 requires — so the driver was inside the geofence at or before the arrival event. (c) He then held position inside the geofence continuously from 08:10:00 to the 08:15:20 cancellation: 320 seconds against the 300-second STANDARD minimum, measured from the first qualifying fix as the clause requires (the derived shortfall of -20 seconds is a 20-second surplus). (d) The trip was terminated by the driver at 08:15:20 with cancellation_reason_code RIDER_NO_SHOW, one of the three codes limb (d) recognises, at the moment the 300-second dwell elapsed, and no boarding event is recorded. Your account that you were 'downstairs' is not borne out by your own device: the rider track places you about 519 m from the pin across all 15 of its fixes. You also sent no message in the app during the waiting window, so POL-NS-04 limb (a) fails and that clause does not exonerate you. POL-NS-03 does not apply (the driver was inside the arrival radius, not at a wrong face of the venue within 400 m). POL-NS-05 does not apply — the 'arrived' marker coincides with a stationary fix at 0 km/h, 24 m from the pin, nowhere near the 300 m or 15 km/h thresholds, so it is not a false marker. POL-NS-06 does not apply — there is no dwell shortfall. The driver's 08:10:35 chat message naming the sheltered pickup point beside Block 310 matches the registered pickup venue, so the pickup point is established on a party statement, not on general geography.\n\nTo the driver: your no-show is verified and your time is compensated. Under POL-NS-07 you receive 80% of the SGD 4.00 fee — SGD 3.20 — with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not trip: driver_profile.no_show_terminations_30d is 1, below the threshold of 4, so the second limb is never reached and compensation is not withheld. The charge itself stands as itemised: the SGD 4.00 cancellation fee reconciles with fee_schedule.resolution_rule as the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), so no POL-NS-08(d) fare defect arises.\n\nEvidence integrity: the traffic advisory EV-ADVIS-09101-01 is MISSING, weight 0.0, issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT; it carries no fact and is not relied upon — the dwell was one single continuous in-geofence run, so no advisory is needed to join intervals, and nothing is asserted against it. Apart from that artifact, no evidence relied upon is impaired under POL-NS-08(a)–(d): there is no clock skew (the 08:10:20 arrival event coincides with a fix), no trace gap (100% coverage, 33 fixes at a 10-second cadence, zero gaps), no chat defect (the log's 3 messages match trip_record.chat_message_count of 3), and no fare defect. No POL-NS-09 escalation trigger is present either: confidence is well above the 0.70 floor, no admissible artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, the same-party dispute counters are both 0, no anti-farming pattern trips, and no deciding fact rests on an impaired artifact. The case is therefore decided on the record. The rule that the fee stands is the disposition of the charge under POL-GEN-03; the outcome this case produces is the driver compensation, so amount_sgd carries the same SGD 3.20 figure as driver_compensation_sgd."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}

{
  "ruling": {
    "ruling": "DRIVER_COMPENSATION",
    "amount_sgd": 3.2,
    "driver_compensation_sgd": 3.2,
    "referrals": [],
    "confidence": 0.95,
    "explanation": "To the rider: your request to reverse the SGD 4.00 cancellation charge is not supported, and the charge stands as it presently is. The platform's record shows the driver reached the pickup point at Blk 310 Clementi Ave 4 (sheltered pickup point), registering an 'arrived' event at 08:10:20. His device stayed about 24 m from the pin throughout — comfortably inside the 50 m arrival radius for a STANDARD pickup — and he held position for 320 seconds, twenty seconds more than the 300 second minimum. He cancelled at 08:15:20 under the reason code RIDER_NO_SHOW with no boarding event recorded. All four conditions the no-show rule requires are therefore met, so the fee is properly chargeable. Your own device placed you roughly 519 m from the pin, which does not bear out the account that you were waiting downstairs, but the outcome does not turn on that: the fee is chargeable whether or not you were present, once the driver's four conditions hold.\n\nTo the driver: you are entitled to compensation of SGD 3.20, being 80 per cent of the SGD 4.00 fee, with SGD 0.80 retained as the platform service fee. The anti-farming check does not bite — you had 1 no-show termination in the trailing 30 days, below the threshold of 4, so the second limb is never reached. The billed amount reconciles under the resolution rule: SGD 4.00 is the greater of the STANDARD zone-class fee (SGD 4.00) and the RYDE_X vehicle-tier fee (SGD 4.00), the two dimensions agreeing, so there is no fare-integrity defect.\n\nThe advocates' positions converge on the same record. Arrival and dwell are conceded on both sides: the trace shows 33 qualifying fixes 24.01 m from the pin from 08:10:00, and a single continuous in-geofence run of 320 seconds against the 300 second STANDARD minimum. None of the rider-protective routes is engaged: there is no wrong-entrance case because the driver was inside the arrival radius, not outside it within the 400 m ceiling; the rider-contact route fails at its first limb because the chat log holds three messages, none from the rider (two from the driver, one system notice) and the log is not truncated, its count matching the trip record; the false-arrival route fails because the driver was stationary at 0 km/h 24 m from the pin, nowhere near the 300 m or 15 km/h thresholds; and the waiting-period-shortfall route fails because the dwell met the minimum, so the missing traffic advisory was not needed to join any intervals — the run was uninterrupted. The traffic advisory artifact EV-ADVIS-09101-01 is MISSING at weight 0.0 (issue code MISSING_ARTIFACT), and I note that no deciding fact rests on it, so it neither caps confidence nor triggers escalation. The trace (100 per cent coverage, 33 fixes at the 10 second cadence, zero gaps, exact alignment with the arrival timestamp) and the trip record are both complete at weight 1.0, so the confidence cap on the deciding facts is 1.0 and no integrity limb of the evidence-integrity clause is engaged. No escalation trigger is present: confidence is above the 0.70 floor, no two artifacts contradict each other on arrival, dwell or rider presence, the repeat-dispute counters are both 0, and no abuse pattern is shown."
  },
  "discarded_claims": []
}
